.TH LINTO 1 "October 2026" "linto" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linto \- dispatch command-line tools from the Linux Tools collection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linto
.RI [ --help ]
.br
.B linto
.I command
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B linto
.I group command
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B linto help
.RI [ page | group [ command ] ]
.br
.B linto completion
.RI { bash | zsh | fish }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linto
is a command dispatcher for the local Linux Tools collection. It locates tools
relative to the
.B linto
launcher, so commands can be run from any working directory. A tool receives
the arguments supplied after its command name.
.PP
With no arguments or with
.BR --help ,
.B linto
prints the available groups and their commands. Running a group by itself
lists its commands. Each command can be run as
.B "linto GROUP COMMAND" .
The unqualified forms
.B "linto SHORTCUT"
and
.B "linto-SHORTCUT"
are available for names explicitly configured in the top-level
.B shortcuts
mapping. Each shortcut maps to a specific group and command. Group-qualified
forms remain available for every active group.
.SH GROUPS
The currently active groups are:
.\" BEGIN GENERATED GROUPS
.BR beta  ,
.BR bib  ,
.BR launch  ,
.BR linto  ,
.BR quarto  ,
and
.BR utils  .
.\" END GENERATED GROUPS
Run a group by itself to list its commands. The
.B launch
group contains the Zed launcher. Use a group followed by a command to run a
tool explicitly, for example
.BR "linto utils prettyprint" .
Use a configured shortcut name for an unqualified command, or use the group and
command explicitly.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help [PAGE|GROUP [COMMAND]]
Print the guide index with no arguments. A page name displays a topic guide;
.B linto help GROUP
lists a group's commands. With a command name, display that tool's help; a group
may be specified to select the command explicitly. For most commands this runs
the tool with
.BR --help ;
some commands provide dispatcher-specific help instead.
.TP
.B completion SHELL
Print shell completion setup instructions for
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
or
.BR fish .
This prints instructions; it does not modify shell configuration files.
.TP
.I shortcut [arguments ...]
Run the target command configured for this shortcut in the top-level
.B shortcuts
mapping.
.TP
.I group command [arguments ...]
Run a tool from the specified group. The tool's standard input, output, error,
and exit status are passed through.
.PP
The alias
.B slug
runs
.BR stripaccents .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , --help
Print the usage summary when given as the first argument. To request help for a
specific tool, use
.B "linto SHORTCUT --help"
for a configured shortcut, or use
.BR "linto help GROUP COMMAND" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The dispatcher exits with status 0 when it successfully prints its own help or
completion instructions. Invalid dispatcher usage, an unsupported completion
shell, or an unknown command results in status 2. For a dispatched command,
.B linto
returns that command's exit status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the available commands:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto --help
.RE
.fi
.PP
List commands in a group:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto quarto
.RE
.fi
.PP
Extract unique citation keys from a Quarto document as a numbered YAML map,
ordered by first appearance (the default):
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto quarto citations report.qmd
.RE
.fi
.PP
Write the keys as CSV, sorted alphabetically:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto quarto citations --order-by key --format csv report.qmd
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run a tool with or without its group:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto quarto render --help
.RE
.fi
.PP
Open a file with the Zed tool:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto zed Makefile
.RE
.fi
.PP
Print the Bash completion setup line:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto completion bash
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I linto
The command dispatcher.
.TP
.I linto-guide/
The multi-page guide shown by
.BR "linto help" . Topic pages are selected with
.BR "linto help PAGE" .
.TP
.I completions/linto.bash
.TQ
.I completions/linto.zsh
.TQ
.I completions/linto.fish
Shell completion definitions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR zsh (1),
.BR fish (1)
